[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=0.5,ystep=0.25] (0,0) grid (6,4.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.6,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/200,2/400,3/600,4/800} {\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\x$};}
\draw[red,thick] (0,0)--(6,4.2);
\draw[blue,dashed,<-] (0,3.5)--(5,3.5);
\draw[blue,dashed,<-] (5,0)--(5,3.5);
\fill[blue] (5,3.5) circle (2pt);
\node[font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (2.4,3.85) {$700$};
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-2,2) {Interest (dollars)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-1) {Time (years)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3,5.1) {Study savings account};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Read up from $5$ years to the line, then across to the interest axis.
$I = \$700.00$
$I = Prn$
$\$700 = \$4000 \times r \times 5$
$\$700 = \$20\,000 \times r$
$r = \frac{700}{20\,000}$
$= 0.035$
$= 3.5\%\text{ p.a.}$
